# @hsk-sync:new-note

Token `@hsk-sync:new-note` marks one logical **New note** command in three places. If behavior, beginning templates, or personal-data settings change in any implementation, update the other two to match.

## Sibling implementations

| Block | Path |
|-------|------|
| Python action | `src/harrix_swiss_knife/actions/markdown/new_markdown.py` (`OnNewMarkdown` new-note path) |
| Beginning snippets | `config/beginning-of-*.md` + `personal_data` in `config.json` / `config.example.json` |
| VS Code (JS) | `vscode/harrix-notes-explorer-hsk/new-note.js` + `harrixNotesExplorerHsk.newNote.*` / `personalData.*` in `package.json` |
| Android | `D:\GitHub\harrix-notes-android` — create note + New note settings (`NotesTreeRepository`, `NotesViewerPreferences`, `SettingsScreen`, `NotesCreateNoteDialog`) |

## Shared contract

1. Choose a beginning template (picker when interactive; default/first otherwise).
2. Body: beginning text + `\n# {heading}\n\n\n`.
3. `personal_data.enabled` default **false** — omit `author` / `author-email` when off; inject configured values when on (defaults `noname` / empty).
4. Desktop/JS filename stem: spaces → `-`, `-` → `--`; layout `{folder}/{stem}/{stem}.md`.
5. Android may keep SAF single-file layout; **content** must match the contract.

Out of scope for this sync id: Diary/Dream/Cases, rich `markdown_templates` (Coffee/Travel/…).

Later synced commands use their own `@hsk-sync:<id>` + rule file using this pattern.
